cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "This is an untagged scientific-revision candidate; cite a released version when available."
title: "EXOTIC-CCR A001: Poisson/Weyl lifts and Lean-backed dual-transport deficiency theory"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Fredriksen
    given-names: Daniel Eric
    affiliation: "Quantyra Inc"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21474351
version: "0.3.9-referee-revision"
url: "https://github.com/Quantyra/jacobian-weyl-quantum-phase-space"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Quantyra/jacobian-weyl-quantum-phase-space"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - jacobian-conjecture
  - deficiency-indices
  - essential-self-adjointness
  - exotic-ccr
abstract: >-
  Proposed, untagged targeted revision of the A001 paper package. For the
  canonical real dual transport operator H=-i X_1 associated with the
  restated Alpoge-Fable Keller seed, the paper gives Hilbert deficiency
  indices n_+=n_-=aleph0. The revised main proof constructs the minus-i
  family from a forward maximal sheet and obtains the plus-i family through
  the measure-preserving sign involution. The synchronized Lean publication
  freeze is b8bc72ea87531b88d50ed588ec6268ae743a662f; it is untagged and
  unreleased. The historical theorem-source root is
  ff50f4a2a312591c2e5b26e71eb390ade9164b34. Math.FA, math.AG, Lean/build,
  and non-claims gates pass; package/metadata recheck and Dan approval remain
  pending. Lean proves the exact aleph0 Hilbert-basis
  indices, the bounded canonical-core Theorems E-F, a bijective von Neumann
  classification for the specific H_X1_min, and an injective family of
  distinct self-adjoint-extension witnesses parameterized by unitary complex
  phases. This exhibits a continuum-sized lower family but does not identify
  the exact cardinality of the full extension type. No preferred extension,
  arbitrary-operator theorem, exact Hamel rank, strong CCR, physical selection,
  or rank-three Dixmier counterexample is claimed. The backward
  wall is retained as independent paper geometry and is not used in the main
  deficiency proof. Prior withdrawn claims remain documented in the erratum.
